<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Sun Beam</h1>
<p>Sphere: Fire Sphere
Class: none (no guild teaches it)
Mana: 15
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast sun beam &lt;target&gt;
<a cmd='#'>cast sun beam</a>   (at whoever you are fighting)
use a wand or staff of sun beam
</pre>
<p>The caster calls to the shining rays of the sun for power, and a beam of 
sunlight burns the target. It is meant to work only outdoors, in daylight, 
under a clear or cloudy sky. It is strongest at noon and weaker towards 
dawn and dusk, and it burns the undead far worse than the living.
</p><p>It does about as well against any armour, and a shield softens it. Casting 
it is an attack and starts a fight. No guild teaches it, but it turns up on 
wands and staffs among random treasure.
</p><p>Note: at present the spell always fails with "The heavy rain clouds block 
any chance of casting the spell", whatever the weather. This is a known 
bug.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
